WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.190
- Okay, so I have to know about this.

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:06.100
I heard, my producers are telling me,

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:08.486
did you steal a sandwich from someone

00:00:08.486 --> 00:00:09.411
at some point?
- Yeah, I sure did.

00:00:09.411 --> 00:00:11.400
And you ended up like literally in jail?

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:12.817
- Yeah, I sure did.

00:00:12.817 --> 00:00:14.050
When I was-
- I gotta know this story,

00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:16.170
'cause that's an awesome story.

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:17.003
- Yeah.

00:00:17.003 --> 00:00:18.580
I was, I think I was 18 years
old, well, I was 18 years old.

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:22.760
I was in my freshman year in
college and I had no money

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:24.520
and, like zero money.

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:27.951
I don't know how I even bought a book.

00:00:27.951 --> 00:00:29.760
- That was me at 18 as well, yes.

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:30.593
- Right?

00:00:30.593 --> 00:00:33.410
And so we were, we all went out one night,

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:36.260
and we were walking back from a party,

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:39.010
and there was a kind of
like a, not 7-Eleven,

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:40.690
but a 7-Eleven type store,

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:42.550
and so we walked in and I was like,

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:44.370
oh my God, I'm starving,
I haven't eaten all day.

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:46.090
And I stole a turkey sandwich.

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:49.670
And so I walked outside with my friends

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:51.180
and I'm like, ew, it has tomatoes on it.

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:52.920
So we started throwing
tomatoes in the street

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:55.620
because we were dorks and losers,

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:58.220
and then I'm eating it,
and we're all laughing,

00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:01.480
and comes up a cop, stands
right in front of me.

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:04.120
And I just see like his badge,
and I look up to his face.

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:05.690
He's like, "You need to come with me."

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:07.080
And I'm like, "Are you joking me?"

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:07.970
He's like, "No."

00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:10.730
So I get in the cop car,
I had to go to jail.

00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:12.530
This kid bailed me out, his name was Liam.

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:14.370
He was the nicest guy, I didn't know him.

00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:15.500
And he gave me the 100 bucks.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:17.270
- You didn't know him
and he bailed you out?

00:01:17.270 --> 00:01:18.920
- Yeah, because it was part of like,

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:20.550
you know, it was freshman year in college.

00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:21.850
Everybody's kinda meeting everybody.

00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:24.520
So I didn't know him that well,
like I, but he was so nice.

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:26.300
And so I borrowed the 100 dollars

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:29.470
from my brother the next
day, and I paid him back,

00:01:29.470 --> 00:01:32.800
and then cut to, I don't
know how many years later,

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:36.580
I'm in Los Angeles and I'm at
a cafe and the guy comes up,

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:38.790
my waiter, and he goes,
"Do you remember me?"

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:40.130
I was like, "No."

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:43.410
He goes, "I'm Liam, I
bailed you out of jail."

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:44.243
- No way!

00:01:44.243 --> 00:01:45.250
- I was like, wait, what?

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:46.083
That's so crazy.

00:01:46.083 --> 00:01:47.640
'Cause I hadn't seen
him after he did that.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:50.160
He like transferred schools
or something or left.

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:51.890
And isn't that crazy?

00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:52.723
- That is crazy.

00:01:52.723 --> 00:01:54.750
Well, what's crazier is I
have a surprise for you.

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:57.350
Liam, come on in the Zoom room!

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:59.263
No, I'm just kidding, no! (laughs)

00:01:59.263 --> 00:02:02.650
- Could you, could you
imagine, could you imagine?

00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:04.990
- I was just kidding, I just
wanted to see your bluff face,

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:05.930
and by the way, it looks like this.

00:02:05.930 --> 00:02:06.763
Oh, (beep).

00:02:06.763 --> 00:02:09.420
- Yeah. (laughs)

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:10.253
- All right.

00:02:10.253 --> 00:02:11.086
I'm just kidding.

00:02:11.086 --> 00:02:12.140
I was checking your poker face,

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:13.680
we don't have Liam.
- Yeah, no, I have none.

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:14.513
- I have none.

00:02:14.513 --> 00:02:15.730
But if you brought Liam on,

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:17.920
that would be the best surprise ever.

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:19.703
I've always wondered what happened to him.

